# Detection: Multiple failed logons (brute force)
# Alert name: Brute Force - Multiple Failed Logons (T1110.001)
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.001 (Brute Force: Password Guessing)
# Log source: Windows Security, EventCode 4625
# Schedule: every 5 minutes (cron */5 * * * *), 10-minute lookback
# Trigger: number of results > 0, for each result
# Throttle: suppress by target_user for 30 minutes
# False positives: user mistyping a password repeatedly; service
#   account with an outdated stored password
# Tuning history:
#   v1: no tight time window and no throttling. 11 duplicate alerts
#       from a single test.
#   v2: 10-minute lookback and per-user suppression. 1 alert per attack.

index=main EventCode=4625 earliest=-10m
| eval target_user=mvindex(Account_Name,1)
| stats count, min(_time) as first_seen, max(_time) as last_seen by target_user, Source_Network_Address, host
| where count >= 5
